Security follow-on backlog - defects and gaps found while fixing the three
reported findings


1. WHAT THIS IS AND WHAT IT IS NOT

   Every item below was found while fixing the three reported findings (the
   unauthenticated help.php file read, the authenticated relay SQL-injection
   cluster, and the vcalendar pass-the-hash path) on branch
   security/mitigation-2026-09 at HEAD f0aeba53. None of them is part of that
   mitigation. Each is either out of scope by decision (section 2) or a
   pre-existing defect that the sweep, its reviews and the verification pass
   surfaced on the way (sections 3 to 6). Nothing here has been fixed. Every
   file:line reference was re-read at f0aeba53 while this list was consolidated,
   and every claim that could be measured without a database was measured on
   php:8.3-cli; references the plan or the execution ledger carried that have
   since drifted are corrected here, and each correction is stated inline. Where
   a claim rests on a single measurement, or on a review's assertion that this
   consolidation did not re-measure, the line says so. The advisory for the
   mitigation itself is a separate delivery (Task 4.2): nothing here duplicates
   it, and nothing here has been sent outside this repository.


2. OUT OF SCOPE BY DECISION

   These are not defects the mitigation skipped. They are changes of a different
   shape and size, each of which needs its own reviewed plan.

   2.1 Credential storage: unsalted MD5 -> password_hash() / PASSWORD_BCRYPT
       (CWE-916). Every stored credential is an unsalted MD5 digest, and the
       digest is compared in six places: User.class.php:354 and :446
       (set/change), Authentication_Password.class.php:34,
       Authentication_Basic.class.php:35, public/Login.class.php:116
       (md5($password) == $row), public/Installation.class.php:105,
       api/UserInterface.class.php:413 and :548, and vcalendar.php:89. The
       mitigation only removed the comparison from SQL in vcalendar.php (it now
       fetches by username and compares in PHP with hash_equals()) and left the
       format alone; the format is why the pass-the-hash item exists at all, and
       Authentication_Password.class.php:34 still accepts a client-supplied
       `_hash` in place of a password. Changing the storage format is a
       migration - rehash on next successful login, a dual-format acceptance
       window, the GWT login, and a decision about accounts that never log in
       again - not a patch.

   2.2 Library-wide prepared statements. The mitigation parameterized by the
       established idiom on the reachable and in-scope surface (->quote() for
       values, intval()/casts for numeric ids, a validated-identifier helper for
       schema and column names; the plan counted 252 pre-existing ->quote( sites
       setting the precedent, and the sweep added more). Moving the whole
       library to prepared statements is a rewrite
       with its own regression surface, and the identifier half of the problem
       cannot be bound at all - it still needs a validator.

   2.3 The vendored phpGACL/adodb copies under
       lib/org/freemedsoftware/acl/ (notably acl/adodb/). Their string
       concatenation is library-internal and upstream-maintained: note it, do
       not fork it. 67 of the concatenation gate's 76 remaining allowlist
       entries are third-party phpGACL lines, and the .htaccess inside that
       directory is deliberately left 2.2-only for the same reason.

   2.4 The legacy lib/agata7/ surface (73 of the gate's 165 originally
       allowlisted lines: bundled fpdf151, pclzip and nusoap). Vendored
       third-party code, out of scope by the plan's non-goals; its entries sit
       in the allowlist's VENDORED section rather than in the application set
       the sweep had to zero.


3. PRE-EXISTING FUNCTIONAL DEFECTS THE SWEEP AND ITS REVIEWS SURFACED

   All are pre-existing; none was introduced by the mitigation. "Live" means an
   in-tree caller or a shipped file reaches it. "Latent" means it is reachable
   in principle but nothing in the tree currently gets there.

   3.1 The eight the plan listed

   a) lib/org/freemedsoftware/core/SupportModule.class.php:557
      FormJoinClause()'s `if ( ($k+0) == 0 )` treats every module-declared join
      key as an integer. With a string key PHP 8 raises `TypeError: Unsupported
      operand types: string + int` (measured). Two modules declare one -
      module/UserGroups.class.php:57 and module/ShimStation.class.php:59 - and
      the committed smoke baseline records that exact TypeError as UserGroups'
      own EXC entry, so this is LIVE for them: the 2.6b-validated JOIN path can
      never run on those two modules, and it could only be measured with a
      numeric key.

   b) lib/org/freemedsoftware/api/FormTemplate.class.php:419
      ProcessData() (:339-530) calls $GLOBALS['sql']->num_rows($result).
      FreemedDb (lib/org/freemedsoftware/core/FreemedDb.class.php) implements no
      num_rows() and reaches no __call, so the call is `Error: Call to
      undefined method` - after the statement has been built and executed.
      Latent on the shipped tree: no XML template ships, so that path cannot be
      driven live (a limit Task 2.8 round 2 discloses about its own gating).

   c) lib/org/freemedsoftware/api/Scheduler.class.php:1462
      ImportDate()'s (:1455) `m/d/Y` case reads
      preg_match("/([0-9]{1,2})/([0-9]{1,2})/([0-9]{2,4})/", ...) - the `/`
      delimiters are unescaped, so PCRE takes the second `/` as the closing
      delimiter and `(` as a modifier: `Warning: preg_match(): Unknown modifier
      '('`, and the case never matches (measured: preg_match returns false).
      This is why the F4 date validation refuses that format instead of letting
      it become a zero date. CORRECTION: the plan attributed this method to
      vcalendar.php; it is defined in api/Scheduler.class.php and reached from
      EMRModule.class.php:884.

   d) lib/org/freemedsoftware/module/PaymentModule.class.php:750-753
      ledger() walks $GLOBALS with reset()/each(); each() was removed in PHP 8
      (measured: `Error: Call to undefined function each()`), so the method
      fatals on its first statement and everything after it in the method is
      unreachable. Dead code with no caller - a deletion candidate, not a patch.

   e) lib/org/freemedsoftware/module/Callin.class.php:159-163
      GetAllWithInsurance() guards on $criteria['cifname'] (:159) but composes
      `ci.cilname like <$criteria['cilname']>` (:163) - the wrong column AND the
      wrong value, so a cifname criterion is silently ignored. Behaviour is
      deliberately unchanged (fixing it changes results). CORRECTION: the plan's
      `:142` is stale; the sweep shifted this block.

   f) lib/org/freemedsoftware/core/Relay_Json.class.php:58
      deserialize_request() calls urldecode($request) where $request may be an
      array: `TypeError: urldecode(): Argument #1 ($string) must be of type
      string, array given` (measured). Latent, and deliberately left alone:
      the JSON-body path already fatals earlier at :87/:90, and repairing this
      would re-open that transport mid-verification (ruling R11). See 4.3.

   g) lib/org/freemedsoftware/core/class.IIGAlert.php:49
      Parse error (measured: php -l reports `syntax error, unexpected string
      content ""` at :49, the "$row['pc_eventDate']" interpolation), plus the
      removed mysql_* API at :31, :46, :47, :79 and :83 - and no caller. The
      cleanest resolution is deletion, not a patch.

   h) lib/org/freemedsoftware/module/PaymentModule.class.php:779
      splices `(string) $this->view_query` into a statement. Nothing in the tree
      assigns that property (the sibling method uses a *local* $view_query with
      an explicit whitelist at :1149-1183), so it contributes the empty string
      and warns on the undefined property - but it becomes a live raw splice the
      moment a caller assigns it. CORRECTION: the plan's `:768` is stale. It
      also sits inside the dead ledger() of (d), so at HEAD it cannot execute
      either.

   3.2 Found later, in the sweep's reviews and the vcalendar work

   i) lib/API.php:938-961 - freemed::secure_filename() is a NO-OP. Its search
      strings are built as "\$".$secure_var, i.e. the literal sequences `$\`,
      `$.`, `$/` and `$|`, instead of the four characters the comment claims to
      remove, so str_replace never strips `../` or a separator (measured:
      secure_filename('../../etc/passwd') returns its input unchanged). Two
      sinks trust it:

        * module/UpdatesModule.class.php:124 (GetFeed()) composes
          data/cache/rss.feed.<feed> from the relay-supplied $feed. The read is
          real through an authenticated relay call, but the content is not
          reflected into the response, and its confinement today is accidental
          (the `$`-prefixed component cannot exist as a directory).
        * core/BaseModule.class.php:165-166 - the
          $_REQUEST['print_template'] override check and use (not measured).
          The plan calls this sink `BaseModule::print_template`; the containing
          method is _print() (:121-313).

      Four further callers inherit the no-op: module/UnfiledDocuments.class.php
      :170, module/UnreadDocuments.class.php:246,
      module/ScannedDocuments.class.php:124-125 and lib/API.php:1085. NOT fixed
      here, because the fix changes which file names callers may use. Found by
      Task 1.3; recorded in tests/security/evidence/path-sink-audit.md.

   j) controller.php:48 - strtolower(${layout}) parses `${layout}` as "the
      variable named by the CONSTANT layout", which on PHP 8 is `Uncaught
      Error: Undefined constant "layout"` (measured: php -r
      'strtolower(${layout});', and the live /controller.php/Dojo/default in
      path-sink-audit.md). Every request whose layout passes the alpha check at
      :43 fatals there, before either include_once (:54/:68); a bare
      /controller.php still answers 200 "Hack attempt, dying", because :43
      rejects the empty layout first. Pre-existing, and on no path the
      mitigation touched.

   k) lib/org/freemedsoftware/core/Physician.class.php:83-88 - fullName() hands
      the degrees ROW ARRAY to strpos(): `TypeError: strpos(): Argument #1
      ($haystack) must be of type string, array given` (measured). $e is set at
      :81 from get_link('degrees', ...), so ANY provider who has degrees breaks
      this method - app-wide across its callers, and it is exactly the blocker
      for demonstrating a populated vCalendar body on the path Tasks 3.1/3.2
      secured. The bounded count() guard and the !empty($d) refinement this
      mitigation added live in the same method (:97-98, :104, :111) and do not
      address it.

   l) lib/org/freemedsoftware/core/vCalendar.class.php:58 - generate() uses
      $buffer .= before $buffer is initialised, so PHP 8 emits `Warning:
      Undefined variable $buffer` (measured) on the first concatenation and
      prints it INTO the payload when display_errors is on; production's
      display_errors=Off is the only reason the body is clean. A malformed body
      is a functional defect, not a leak. CORRECTION: the plan's `:61` is stale;
      the first uninitialised use is :58 (the PRODID line the plan pointed at is
      :61).

   m) freemed::acl() is unusable outside a session-enabled request.
      lib/API.php:57-75 dereferences $GLOBALS['acl']->acl_check(...), and
      $GLOBALS['acl'] is only built by lib/acl.php:28, which lib/freemed.php
      includes at :185 - inside the session block guarded at :113 by
      !defined('SESSION_DISABLE'). A SESSION_DISABLE entrypoint (vcalendar.php,
      and any future Basic-auth endpoint) therefore gets a null ACL, and
      acl_check() on null is a fatal. Task 3.2 works around it (loads the ACL on
      demand, DENIES when it is unusable - correct fail-closed behaviour), but
      the consequence stands: an authorised non-physician scheduler also gets
      403 on a deployment whose ACO/ARO grant rows are not seeded. The
      structural fix - an ACL that does not depend on a session - belongs in its
      own change.

   n) vcalendar.php:85 (Basic auth) and :151 (the deprecated GET-hash path,
      reached only with vcals_legacy_hash on) splice the authenticating username
      with addslashes($user) inside hand-written quotes, for an
      attacker-controlled, PRE-AUTHENTICATION value. It is safe on this
      deployment only because the server's sql_mode lacks NO_BACKSLASH_ESCAPES
      and FreemedDb issues no SET sql_mode / SET NAMES: with that mode set, a
      crafted username reaches a UNION SELECT row whose digest the attacker
      chooses, which resolves to an id / userrealphy of their choosing - admin
      to any provider's calendar. It is the exact idiom the sweep's brief
      prescribed (->quote() here), so it was routed rather than re-fixed in
      place. CORRECTION: the plan's `:73-74` is stale.

   o) vcalendar.php:164 - freemed_get_auth() (:138) ends with a `return false;`
      after an if/else whose branches both return (:160 and :162). Unreachable
      statement, cosmetic only; the legacy GET path leaves with the D4 window.

