5. WEB AND CONFIGURATION RESIDUALS

   5.1 ui/dojo/htdocs/.htaccess is still 2.2-only (`allow from all` / `order
       allow,deny`). On an Apache 2.4 without mod_access_compat that is a
       configuration error during URI mapping - a 500-shaped failure on the
       world-readable Dojo tree, not the 403 the shipped server rule promises
       (the server-config deny does not run first). Deferred by ruling R35 to
       the final fix pass, because the failure needs a non-default Apache build;
       the fix is the same module-guarded dual-syntax block Task 4.1 applied to
       the five sibling files (data/, data/schema/, data/config/,
       data/documents/unfiled/, tests/). Measured at config level only: without
       mod_access_compat `apache2 -t` rejects the old form with `Invalid command
       'order'` and accepts the new ones (a review confirmed this against the
       image's module set minus that module under MINOR-6).
       lib/org/freemedsoftware/acl/.htaccess is deliberately left 2.2-only as
       vendored phpGACL (R34/R14).

   5.2 The repository-root ./.htaccess guards its `DirectoryIndex index.php`
       with <IfModule mod_php5.c>, which is inert on every supported PHP (the
       module is php_module / php7_module / php8_module), so the directive never
       takes effect - an ineffective guard of the same class as the `deny from
       *` files Task 4.1 replaced. Deferred with 5.1 by R35. It is the only file
       in the tree whose .htaccess carries no deny rule at all.

   5.3 doc/freemed.apache.conf has two <Directory "/usr/share/freemed">
       sections (:22-30, the base allow-all + AcceptPathInfo On + AllowOverride
       All block, and :213-222, the mod_rewrite PATH_INFO refusal). The
       execution ledger records, from the Task 4.1 re-review, that a
       later-loaded block for the same path REPLACES rather than merges the
       earlier rule set, direction fail-open; the shipped config has exactly one
       such duplicate path. RECORDED, NOT RE-MEASURED here - this consolidation
       did not test Apache's merge semantics for a duplicated <Directory> path,
       so treat the direction as unverified until someone does.

   5.4 Two .htaccess-layer behaviours could not be measured in this
       environment at all: a real Apache 2.2 (the old syntax half) and a real
       Apache 2.4 with mod_access_compat absent serving requests. Everything
       measured for 5.1 is config-test level plus the two repo-mounted servers
       that ship the image's module set minus that one module. Anything built on
       the .htaccess layer in future should say which of the two halves it
       actually exercised.


6. EVIDENCE-QUALITY AND HARNESS RESIDUALS CARRIED FORWARD

   6.1 The module-smoke functional gate cannot see a valid-but-wrong query that
       returns 0 rows. The committed baseline is 136 entries - OK 6, EXC 22,
       SKIP 108 (tests/security/evidence/module-smoke-before.json) - and the
       108 SKIPs come from the reduced seed: the harness's empty tables make a
       correct query and a wrong-but-valid query indistinguishable. After Task
       2.6d the query builder really runs for 18 more modules (a broken query
       now surfaces as `EXC: GetList() returned DB_Error`), so the residual is
       narrower than it was - but "0 deltas" is not proof that a batch's SQL is
       equivalent, only that the observables did not move.

   6.2 The relay allowlist ships log-only (enforce = false in
       data/config/relay-allowlist.php). Its 323-pattern call set was enumerated
       from source, from this work's own live probes and from a retained access
       log (tests/security/evidence/relay-callset.txt, generated at c6c4f306),
       but it was never exercised by a real client session: there is no compiled
       GWT client in the tree (`find ui/gwt -name '*.js'` returns only the
       vendored viewerjs/mugshot resources). Enforcement is therefore proven
