7. HOW TO PICK THIS UP

   Read tests/security/evidence/ first - seed-fingerprint.md before re-running
   any smoke measurement, then sweep-notes.md, path-sink-audit.md,
   relay-callset.txt, relay-allowlist.txt, deployment-hardening.txt and the two
   redacted pre-fix transcripts - alongside the two operator notes this
   mitigation shipped (doc/DEPLOYMENT_HARDENING, doc/RELAY_ALLOWLIST) and
   doc/VCALENDAR_AUTHENTICATION for the one behaviour change clients must know
   about. Then write ONE PLAN PER GROUP rather than one giant change: the
   credential-storage migration (2.1) and the ACL-without-a-session change (3.2
   m) each touch every caller of a shared interface and need their own gates;
   the sanitizer and value-splice family (3.2 i, 3.2 n, 3.3 q) is a correctness
   change to what callers may pass and needs the callers' agreement first; the
   PHP 8.3 fatals (3.1 a-f, 3.3 p) are mostly deletions and bounded guards and
   can be taken together; the config and .htaccess residuals (5) are
   independent of both and the cheapest. Nothing in this file authorises a
   change to code, tests, configuration or .htaccess on its own, and every
   reference here should be re-read against HEAD before it is acted on.
